# Stock pipeline project

Containerized ETL: Airflow 2.10 (LocalExecutor) + PostgreSQL 15 + Alpha Vantage `GLOBAL_QUOTE`.

## Layout

- `dags/fetch_stock_data_dag.py` — hourly DAG; runs `python /opt/airflow/scripts/fetch_and_store.py` via subprocess
- `scripts/fetch_and_store.py` — fetch, parse, insert into `stock_data`
- `initdb/init.sql` — creates `stock_data` on first Postgres boot only
- `docker-compose.yml` — `postgres`, `airflow-webserver`, `airflow-scheduler`

## Environment

- Secrets and config live in repo-root `.env` (never commit). Use `.env.example` as template.
- Compose substitutes `${POSTGRES_*}` and `${AIRFLOW_ADMIN_PASSWORD}` from `.env`.
- `airflow-scheduler` loads `.env` via `env_file`; task subprocess inherits `ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY`, `STOCK_SYMBOLS`, Postgres vars.
- In containers: `POSTGRES_HOST=postgres`, script path `/opt/airflow/scripts/fetch_and_store.py`.

## Code conventions

- Match existing style: minimal comments, `logging` not print, fail loudly on DB errors.
- Alpha Vantage free tier: keep `time.sleep(12)` between symbols; do not remove without rate-limit plan.
- DAG changes: `schedule_interval` cron in DAG file; tickers via `STOCK_SYMBOLS` in `.env`.
- After `requirements.txt` or Dockerfile changes: `docker compose up --build -d`.
- Do not add real API keys to repo, DAGs, or rules.

## Common pitfalls

- `init.sql` does not re-run if `postgres_data` volume exists — reset volume to recreate schema.
- Web UI: `http://localhost:8080`, user `admin`, password from `AIRFLOW_ADMIN_PASSWORD`.
